---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const asideLinks = [
  { label: 'Our target', href: '#our-target' },
  { label: 'What is implemented', href: '#what-is-implemented' },
  { label: 'Known limitations', href: '#known-limitations' },
  { label: 'Report a barrier', href: '#report-a-barrier' },
  { label: 'Assessment status', href: '#assessment-status' },
];
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  metaTitle="Accessibility: Target, Measures and Feedback"
  description="FixProblemNow aims for WCAG 2.2 AA. Read the accessibility measures, known limitations and how to report a barrier with the site."
  canonical="/accessibility/"
  eyebrow="Accessibility"
  intro="The site targets WCAG 2.2 level AA. This page explains what has been implemented, where limitations remain, and how to report a barrier that affects you."
  updated="2026-11-15"
  asideLinks={asideLinks}
  asideNote="This page describes the current implementation. It is not a claim of certified conformance."
>
  <h2 id="our-target">Our target</h2>
  <p>
    FixProblemNow aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. The
    target applies to the public pages: guides, category pages, search, forms, policies, and the
    site navigation. It does not automatically apply to third-party sites linked from a guide.
  </p>
  <p>
    Accessibility is treated as part of the build rather than a separate add-on. The site is
    designed to work with a keyboard, a screen reader, enlarged text, reduced motion, and a narrow
    viewport.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-is-implemented">What is implemented</h2>
  <ul class="icon-list">
    <li>
      <Icon name="check" size={18} />
      <div>
        <strong>Semantic structure</strong>
        <span>One main landmark, a skip link, descriptive headings, lists, tables with headers, and labelled navigation regions.</span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Icon name="check" size={18} />
      <div>
        <strong>Keyboard access</strong>
        <span>Menus, accordions, search suggestions and forms can be operated without a mouse. Focus is always visible.</span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Icon name="check" size={18} />
      <div>
        <strong>Colour and text</strong>
        <span>Body text and controls are checked for contrast. Text can be enlarged without a fixed-height layout clipping content.</span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Icon name="check" size={18} />
      <div>
        <strong>Forms</strong>
        <span>Every field has a visible label, errors are announced and linked to the field, and success is only shown after a real server response.</span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Icon name="check" size={18} />
      <div>
        <strong>Motion and zoom</strong>
        <span>Animations respect the reduced-motion preference, and layouts reflow at 320 CSS pixels without horizontal scrolling.</span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Icon name="check" size={18} />
      <div>
        <strong>Search</strong>
        <span>The search field exposes combobox semantics, keyboard navigation, an announced result count, and a visible no-results state.</span>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="known-limitations">Known limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Some guides include tables with technical values. On very narrow screens these tables scroll
      horizontally inside a labelled container rather than shrinking the text.
    </li>
    <li>
      Third-party manufacturer pages linked from guides may not meet the same accessibility standard.
    </li>
    <li>
      Search suggestions are enhanced with JavaScript. Without JavaScript, the search form still
      submits to the search page, but live suggestions are unavailable.
    </li>
    <li>
      The site does not provide a fully audited screen-reader experience for every combination of
      browser and assistive technology. Testing is ongoing, and reported barriers are prioritised.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="report-a-barrier">Report a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    If a page is difficult or impossible to use, use the
    <a href="/contact/?topic=accessibility">contact form</a> and choose the accessibility topic.
    Please include the page URL, the task you were trying to complete, the browser and assistive
    technology you used, and what happened. Do not send personal files unless they are needed and
    safe to share.
  </p>

  <h2 id="assessment-status">Assessment status</h2>
  <p>
    The site has been built and checked against the WCAG 2.2 AA success criteria using automated
    checks, keyboard testing, responsive checks, and manual review of the main templates. This is
    not a formal third-party audit or a certification. The page will be updated if an independent
    assessment is completed or if a known limitation is resolved.
  </p>
  <p>
    See also the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for content standards and the
    <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for how contact details are handled.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
